// markdownlint-cli2 configuration for claude-aws-architect.
// Per SPEC §N14.
//
// Rules deliberately relaxed:
// - MD013 (line-length): plugin docs include long descriptive sentences,
//   table rows with rationale columns, and inline links that exceed 80
//   chars. Soft-wrap is preferred over hard-wrap for prose.
// - MD024 (no-duplicate-header): the spec uses repeated `## H2` headings
//   across different sections (e.g. "Required references", "Required
//   templates" appear under multiple skills).
// - MD033 (no-inline-html): we use HTML comments and the occasional
//   <details>/<summary> for collapsible sections.
// - MD034 (no-bare-urls): some examples and links are intentionally bare
//   for copy-paste convenience.
// - MD041 (first-line-h1): ADRs and some templates may start with
//   frontmatter rather than an H1.
// - MD060 (table-column-style): markdown tables in this repo do not enforce
//   pipe alignment — the source-of-truth is GitHub-rendered output.
// - MD001 (heading-increment): SPEC-v4.md and other planning docs use ####
//   subsections without intermediate ### parents to keep the section numbering
//   aligned with the spec text (e.g. "12.A", "12.B-2", "13.G").
// - MD029 (ordered-list-prefix): the PR roadmap uses non-sequential numbers
//   like "28a", "28b" intentionally; SPEC-v4 reuses the spec's own item IDs.
// - MD036 (no-emphasis-as-heading): SPEC.md uses italic _(pending PR N)_ as a
//   parenthetical status marker, which is a note rather than a heading.
// - MD049 (emphasis-style): SPEC-v4.md uses `**bold**` for emphasis throughout
//   to match the source planning conversation; switching to `__bold__` would
//   diverge from the canonical spec text and add zero reader value.
{
  "default": true,
  "MD013": false,
  "MD024": false,
  "MD033": false,
  "MD034": false,
  "MD041": false,
  "MD060": false,
  "MD001": false,
  "MD029": false,
  "MD036": false,
  "MD049": false
}
